The [original incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) treats the merged date reports as one
problem. The export describes two different problems, but its automatic classification
does not establish the cause of every report. This page describes the **4 October 2026
export**, not the current queue.

## Two causes

- **[Shared parser](https://github.com/macaronipasta/mega-dev/issues/1):** it reads dates month-first even for tenants who write the day first.
  Ambiguous dates can be interpreted as the wrong day.
- **[booking-v3 hint](https://github.com/macaronipasta/mega-dev/issues/2):** the form displays `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants. People follow
  the hint, but the form interprets the entry in the tenant's order.

The table deduplicates by report ID. For reports not flagged by the desk, it uses the
existing classification based on tenant locale, form and channel. That classification
does not read report bodies, so its counts are candidates, not confirmed root causes.

The desk flagged five reports for a different reading. They are set aside for review,
not treated as five confirmed cases of one new bug:

- **R-41202:** an invite for 12 May appeared in the calendar on 11 May.
- **R-41209:** bookings in June were reported one day off.
- **R-41236:** an invite arrived before the booking was made; no one-day shift is stated.
- **R-41344:** people in Lisbon and Toronto received different days for the same meeting.
  Time zones may explain this, but the report does not establish the cause or a defect.
- **R-41620:** Tuesday 6 October appeared as Monday.

<ReviewCauseTable />

The original classifier assigns all five to the parser, giving 379 parser candidates.
The review table sets them aside, leaving 374 parser candidates and 33 hint candidates.
The reports and their grouping need further investigation before the cause and count
of any additional issue can be confirmed.

## Reported engineering update

An engineering update relayed to us says #4471 closed on 5 October, the parser was fixed
with `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`, and the hint will not be fixed because
booking-v3 was retired. These are reported outcomes; this page does not independently
verify a deployment or the retirement.

## Arrival and merge history

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Triage

Reports with the same subject can have different causes, and reports with different
subjects can share a cause. Check the tenant, channel and form before grouping. A change
to the accepted subject-based rule requires a new decision record; this page does not
edit the accepted decision.

